  "question": "VetClinic Project\n\n1) Background / Context\n\nVetClinicDB is a database system designed to efficiently manage and organize veterinary clinic data. It serves as a centralized solution for handling information related to animals, customers, and owners. The system aims to streamline clinic operations and improve customer service by maintaining accurate and accessible records.\n\n2) Objectives\n\n- Provide a user-friendly database solution for veterinary clinics.\n- Enhance the accuracy and accessibility of clinic data.\n- Facilitate efficient management of animal medical histories and treatments.\n- Support financial operations through organized invoice management.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Veterinary Clinics: Primary users who will manage patient data and track medical records.\n- Veterinarians: They will use the system to access patient histories and record treatments.\n- Administrative Staff: Responsible for maintaining the database and handling invoices.\n- Pet Owners: Indirect beneficiaries through improved clinic services.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- Patient Management: Record and manage patient information, including name and date of birth.\n- Medical History Tracking: Maintain detailed records of patient medical histories with admission dates and status.\n- Treatment Management: Document and categorize various treatments available at the clinic.\n- Invoicing: Generate and manage invoices, track payment status, and detail invoice items linked to treatments.\n- Record Linking: Ensure all records (patients, medical histories, treatments, invoices) are interlinked for easy retrieval and management.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: Support a growing number of records as the clinic expands.\n- Usability: Offer an intuitive interface for users to efficiently interact with the database.\n- Data Integrity: Maintain accuracy and consistency across all linked records.\n- Security: Protect sensitive data related to patients and financial transactions.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0168\n\nCREATE TABLE `patient` (\n  `patient_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `date_of_birth` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`patient_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `medical_history` (\n  `history_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `patient_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `admission_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`history_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `medical_history_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`patient_id`) REFERENCES `patient` (`patient_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `treatment` (\n  `treatment_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`treatment_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `invoice` (\n  `invoice_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `patient_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `invoice_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `payment_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`invoice_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `invoice_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`patient_id`) REFERENCES `patient` (`patient_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `invoice_item` (\n  `item_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `invoice_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `treatment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,\n  `unit_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`item_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `invoice_item_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`invoice_id`) REFERENCES `invoice` (`invoice_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `invoice_item_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`treatment_id`) REFERENCES `treatment` (`treatment_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
